body:
Hi,
I want to know how to declare my attributes for faceting ?
I don't want to declare them in my dashboard, because there are generated.
I see the searchParameters options but i d'ont find how to declare the attributes for faceting with instant Search.

when i do: 

var search = instantsearch({
  appId: 'myAppId',
  apiKey: 'MyKey',
  indexName: 'Agoarts',
  searchParameters: {
    facets: [
      'coloris'
    ]
  }
});

There are nothing, i see hts and results, but not my coloris filter.
I have to go through the js api ?
If yes, how to do that with Instant Search and it's widgets ?

Thanks you for your attention :)

comments.body:
Ok good form me with the REST API.

But when i try with the JS client and the setSettings method, like that:

var client = algoliasearch('APPID', 'APPKEY');
var index = client.initIndex('Agoarts');
index.setSettings({attributesForFaceting: ['coloris', 'dimension', 'prixttc']});

Console give me:  AlgoliaSearchError: This method is only available in HTTPS. Why ? 
( my tests are in local).

Thank you for your reactivity.

@clementvp when you run a JS script with the JS client we default to the page protocol for all calls. This is something we can fix for all writes to the API since they need to be done in https.

You can either run this script in node.js OR do this:

``` js
var client = algoliasearch('APPID', 'APPKEY', {protocol: 'https:'});
```

Thanks
